"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs (GS) and Citigroup (C) disclose specific executive committees focused on technology and digital risk governance that report to broader technology risk committees or the Board. GS establishes the 'Digital Risk Office Steering Group' to oversee Engineering risk decisions and regulatory compliance, co-chaired by the CISO, CTO, and Chief Digital Risk Officer, with reporting lines to the Firmwide Technology Risk Committee. Similarly, Citi establishes the 'Chief Information Officer Committee (CIOC)' as an escalation forum for technology senior management, including the CISO, to approve policies and report items to the Board's Technology Committee. Both structures utilize specific C-suite leaders (including CISOs) to steer technical risk execution and policy approval within a hierarchy reporting to higher-level technology governance bodies.",
